# See https://docs.github.com/articles/about-codeowners for syntax.
# Later matches take precedence.

* @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers

# Every path where a mistake is a security bug rather than a defect requires a
# security-focused reviewer. The list is by directory rather than by file
# because the native implementation spreads each concern across several
# sources -- and a new file added to one of these directories should inherit
# the requirement automatically rather than wait for someone to notice.
/src/crypto/            @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers @tamga-sh/security
/src/checkout/          @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers @tamga-sh/security
/src/proof.c            @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers @tamga-sh/security
/src/proof.h            @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers @tamga-sh/security
/src/http/              @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers @tamga-sh/security
/src/tamga_mem.c        @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers @tamga-sh/security
/src/tamga_api.c        @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers @tamga-sh/security

# The frozen ABI. A change here is a compatibility decision, not an
# implementation one.
/include/tamga.h        @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers @tamga-sh/security

# The v1.2.2 harness is kept unmodified on purpose -- it is the ABI proof.
/tests/c/               @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers @tamga-sh/security

/.github/workflows/     @tamga-sh/sdk-maintainers
